description:
Design a 4-bit synchronous up-counter with reset functionality. The counter increments its output by one on each rising edge of the clock signal, unless the reset input is activated, in which case the output is reset to zero. The counter employs two pipeline stages to delay the incrementing operation, ensuring that the output is updated reliably with minimal clock domain issues.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input reset,
    output reg [3:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input reset,
    output reg [3:0] out
);reg [3:0] stage1_out;
reg [3:0] stage2_out;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    stage1_out <= out + 1;
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
    stage2_out <= stage1_out;
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (reset) begin
        out <= 4'b0;
    end else begin
        out <= stage2_out;
    end
end

endmodule

