Design a circuit that performs the Hilbert Transform on a signed n-bit input signal, generating an n-bit output that represents the imaginary part of the transform. The module takes a real-valued input, processes it to produce the imaginary component by calculating differences between specified input pairs, and outputs the result. This implementation is suitable for applications in signal processing, particularly for generating analytic signals or phase-shifted representations.
module top_module(
  input signed [n-1:0] in_real,
  output signed [n-1:0] out_imag
);

code:
module top_module(
  input signed [n-1:0] in_real,
  output signed [n-1:0] out_imag
);parameter n = 4; // number of input signals

// Hilbert Transform function
function [n-1:0] hilbert_transform;
  input signed [n-1:0] x;
  integer i;
  begin
    for (i = 0; i < n; i = i + 2) begin
      hilbert_transform[i] = 0;
      hilbert_transform[i+1] = x[i] - x[i+1];
    end
  end
endfunction

// Compute the imaginary part of the Hilbert transform
assign out_imag = hilbert_transform(in_real);

endmodule

