description:
Design a clock divider circuit that generates a slower clock signal (clk_sys) from an input clock (clk). The output clock toggles its state every 50 million rising edges of the input clock, effectively dividing the input frequency by 50 million. This module is useful for generating clock signals that are required at lower frequencies for various subsystems in larger digital designs.
module top_module(
input clk, 
output reg clk_sys = 0 
);

code:
module top_module(
input clk, 
output reg clk_sys = 0 
);reg [25:0]  div_counter = 0;
 always @(posedge clk) begin
 if(div_counter>=50000000) begin 

 clk_sys <= ~clk_sys; 
div_counter <= 0; 
end else begin 
div_counter <= div_counter + 1; 
end
 end
endmodule

