description:
Develop a 3-to-8 decoder that takes a 3-bit input and an enable signal. When the enable signal is LOW, the output is set to all zeros. When the enable signal is HIGH, the decoder activates one of the eight output lines based on the value of the 3-bit input, ensuring that only one output line is set to HIGH corresponding to the binary representation of the input, while all others remain LOW.
module top_module(
    input [2:0] in,
    input en,
    output reg [7:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [2:0] in,
    input en,
    output reg [7:0] out
);always @(*) begin
    if (en == 1'b0) begin
        out <= 8'b00000000;
    end else begin
        case (in)
            3'b000: out <= 8'b00000001;
            3'b001: out <= 8'b00000010;
            3'b010: out <= 8'b00000100;
            3'b011: out <= 8'b00001000;
            3'b100: out <= 8'b00010000;
            3'b101: out <= 8'b00100000;
            3'b110: out <= 8'b01000000;
            3'b111: out <= 8'b10000000;
        endcase
    end
end

endmodule

